# OpenClaw — Agent Self-Brief

> This document is written for the AI assistant working on this codebase.
> Read it completely before writing a single line of code.
> It supersedes any prior assumptions about what this product is.

---

## What I Am Working On

I am building **OpenClaw** — a factory framework that lets organizations spin up their own AI workforces.

OpenClaw is not a legal tool. It is not an API product. It is not a chatbot.

OpenClaw is the **factory**. Organizations are the **customers**. Their AI workforce is the **product**.

The law firm vertical currently live in this codebase is the first proof-of-concept to validate that the factory pattern works. It is one example of what the factory produces. It is not the factory itself.

---

## The Core Mental Model

```
OPENCLAW FACTORY
│
├── Any organization signs up
├── They describe their domain (legal, IR, HR, biotech, finance...)
├── The factory provisions:
│   ├── A Model Forge workspace (training pipeline)
│   ├── A skill bundle (domain-specific capabilities)
│   ├── A knowledge graph (their data, grounded)
│   ├── A governance layer (human-in-loop, audit trail)
│   └── A deployed AI workforce (live endpoints, callable agents)
│
└── The organization now has an AI workforce
    They did not build it. The factory built it for them.
```

A law firm gets legal clause extractors, intake routers, and specialist agents.
A VC fund gets investor research, outreach drafting, and diligence answering.
A biotech gets protocol generation, literature review, and compliance checking.

Same infrastructure. Different skill bundles. That is the entire business.

