## What Is Actually Built (Current State)

### Live Services (Render.com)

| Service | What it does |
|---|---|
| `openclaw-api` (Express 5, Node.js) | Control plane API — auth, tenants, forge, skills, connectors, knowledge graphs, legal endpoints |
| `openclaw-saas` (React + Vite, Static) | Frontend — dashboard, forge workspace, agent management, skill catalog |
| `openclaw-benchmark` (FastAPI, Python) | ZOA multi-LLM router + Kairos execution engine + L1-L4 benchmark harness |
| `archon-factory` (Node.js) | Skill generation pipeline — prompt → generate → validate → benchmark → catalog |
| `openclaw-db` (PostgreSQL) | 28-table schema covering tenants, skills, forge, governance, connectors, graphs |

### Capabilities Delivered

**1. Multi-Tenant Control Plane**
- Clerk auth (sign-in, sign-up, session management)
- Per-user tenant auto-provisioning on first workspace create
- Per-tenant Docker Gateway on Render (isolated, `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_DIR=/tenants/{id}`)
- Render webhook handler for async status sync (deploy_ended, service_suspended, service_deleted)
- Billing tiers: Free ($0, 1 agent), Pro ($29/mo, 5 agents), Enterprise (custom)

**2. Model Forge (Training Pipeline)**
- Workspaces scoped to a domain (legal, IR, HR, etc.)
- Dataset management: upload, version, document tracking
- Training jobs: `draft → queued → running → completed → deployed`
- Three training modes: `prompt_tuning`, `rag_adaptation`, `fine_tuning`
- Governance policy per tenant: model allowlist, concurrency cap, spend limit, approval gate
- Human approval gate: only tenant owner can approve model versions before deployment
- Kairos dispatch: training jobs sent to Kairos execution engine via structured goal string
- SSE stream: frontend connects to live Kairos run events
- Job monitor: polls Kairos every 30s, updates job status, flags `reforge_suggested`
- Model registry: versioned model artifacts with `candidate → approved` lifecycle
- Deployment endpoints: callable paths per active deployment

**3. Governance Layer**
- Every AI output carries a governance envelope (always — not conditional)
- Fields: `human_review_required` (always true), `privilege_warning`, `not_legal_advice`, `escalation_flag`, `jurisdiction_scope`
- Trace block: `retrieval_used`, `fallback_used`, `model_used`, `latency_ms`, `usage_event_id`
- Lineage block: `asset_version`, `dataset_version`, `eval_run`, `model_eval_accuracy`
- Escalation flag triggers when confidence < 0.70 (strengthens warning, does not create it)
- Model approval gate enforced before any deployment
- Audit trail via `model_usage_events` table

**4. ZOA Multi-LLM Router (100% Free Tier)**
- MANAGER: `meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free` — JSON routing
- WORKER Research: `qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct:free` — 262K context, RAG
- WORKER Reasoning: `nousresearch/hermes-3-llama-3.1-405b:free` — 405B frontier, function calling
- WORKER Vision: `google/gemma-3-27b-it:free` — multimodal, charts, PDFs
- WORKER Write: `cognitivecomputations/dolphin-mistral-24b-venice-edition:free` — uncensored
- PLUMBER Short: `liquid/lfm-2.5-1.2b-instruct:free` — format/merge, pure throughput
- PLUMBER Long: `meta-llama/llama-3.2-3b-instruct:free` — 131K context, long merges
- Rate limit fallback chains per worker type
- All calls: `provider: { sort: 'throughput', allow_fallbacks: true }`

**5. Archon Skill Factory (Zeta Skill Forge)**
- Generates TypeScript skills from plain-English prompts
- Pipeline: `prompt → Qwen3 Coder 480B → tsc validate → fix loop (max 2) → L1-L4 benchmark → catalog`
- L0: TypeScript syntax + export verification
- L1-L4: Benchmark harness via OpenRouter
- Grades: CERTIFIED (catalog), CONDITIONAL (catalog with warning), FAILED (blocked), INCONCLUSIVE (allowed with warning)
- Trigger: `POST /archon/generate { "description": "..." }`
- Self-healing: if L0 fails, calls `/internal/fix` and re-validates (max 2 retries)

**6. Skill Ecosystem**
- 791+ real skills loaded from GitHub `awesome-openclaw-skills`
- 30 categories, 24hr in-process TTL cache
- Manual refresh: `POST /api/skills/refresh`
- Skill contract: every skill declares `requiredConnectors` and `requiredGraphs`
- Benchmark gate on install: CERTIFIED or CONDITIONAL required
- Tenant-installed skills tracked in `tenant_skills` (many-to-many)

**7. Connector Registry**
- AES-256-GCM encrypted credential storage (PBKDF2-derived key, 100k iterations)
- Raw credentials never returned in any API response
- Current adapters: Crunchbase (mock/real), Gmail (Phase 2), LinkedIn (Phase 3)
- Each skill declares which connectors it needs — platform checks authorization on install

**8. Knowledge Graph Manager**
- Per-tenant graphs with document ingestion (PDF, TXT)
- Text chunking: ~512 chars with 50-char overlap
- PostgreSQL `tsvector` full-text search with GIN index
- `ts_rank` ordering on search queries
- Bind graphs to skills — skills query their required graphs at runtime

**9. Legal AI Operating Layer (Proof-of-Concept Vertical)**
- 8 live endpoints: extract-clause, intake, contract, litigation, ip, employment, corporate, next-asset-baseline
- Model chain with fallback: gpt-oss-20b → gpt-oss-120b → lfm-1.2b (with RAG)
- CUAD Legal Clause Dataset v2: 50 examples, 5 clause types, CC BY 4.0
- Eval results: gpt-oss-20b 100% accuracy / 1.000 macro-F1; lfm-1.2b+RAG 100% on test set
- Held-out eval: 92.5% accuracy (n=40, promising, NOT production-ready)
- Playbook v1: 9/10 pass; v2: 6/10 pass, correctness=0.75
- Known gaps: S4 (intake calibration), S6 (employment escalation), S10 (privilege detection)

**10. Frontend (React + Vite)**
- Dark terminal aesthetic: `bg-[#0a0a0f]`, `font-mono`, cyan accent
- Light mode: `.light` class, WCAG AA compliant (muted-foreground at 28% lightness)
- Dark/light toggle with `localStorage` persistence and `aria-label`
- 9-tab Forge workspace: Overview, Datasets, Training, Registry, Deployments, Policies, Explorer, Showcase, Journey
- 5-tab Agent detail: Overview, Skills, Chat, Connectors, Knowledge
- Onboarding checklist (5 steps) with progress tracking
- Dataset Explorer: field schemas, type icons, search, drill-down
- SaaS Showcase: Law Firm LIVE + 3 coming-soon verticals
- Training tab: eval stages, playbook scenarios, gap fix cards

