## How to Work on This Codebase

### Before writing any code
1. Read this file
2. Read the relevant individual MDC in `.cursor/rules/`
3. Check the DB schema before touching any SQL
4. Run `pnpm run typecheck` before committing — must pass

### When adding a route
1. Add operation to `lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml`
2. Run `pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen`
3. Create/extend route file in `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/`
4. Mount in `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/index.ts`
5. Run `pnpm run typecheck`

### When adding a frontend page
1. Create in `artifacts/openclaw-saas/src/pages/`
2. Add `<Route>` in `App.tsx`
3. Add nav link in `Layout.tsx`
4. Use generated hooks from `@workspace/api-client-react`

### When writing copy
- Never: "demo", "legal API", "law firm tool", "API endpoints"
- Always: "live", "AI workforce", "factory framework", "deployed AI workforce"
- The platform is the factory. The organization's AI workforce is the product.

### When writing governance outputs
- `human_review_required` is ALWAYS `true` — never conditional
- Always include `trace` block with `usage_event_id`
- Always include `lineage` block with dataset + eval run reference
- Escalation flag strengthens the warning — it does not create it

### Git
- Correct repo: `fjkiani/openclaw-saas`
- Remote: `https://github.com/fjkiani/openclaw-saas.git`
- Auth: use PAT from user memory
- Always push to `main`
- Never push to `fjkiani/crispro-backend-v3` (wrong repo — already reverted once)
